From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmime: audio path GetObjectInPath for all stages, SetVolume ramp, ConvertPChannel

- GetObjectInPath handles every stage: the audio path itself, the port of a
  channel, the buffer (index 0; the interface is asked of the buffer, so
  IKsPropertySet works), buffer DMOs, the primary buffer, the audio path
  graph and tools, the performance, its graph and tools (index counts the
  tools of the requested class, GUID_All_Objects matches all). The
  interface id is honoured for the performance and the graphs, an unknown
  stage is E_INVALIDARG, a missing object DMUS_E_NOT_FOUND. The tool graph
  is released with the path.
- SetVolume sets the buffer volume, over the duration in milliseconds when
  one is given (a timer ramps the volume; a later SetVolume replaces the
  ramp).
- ConvertPChannel: the channels of a path are the first ones of the
  performance (DMUS_E_NOT_FOUND when the performance has no such channel,
  broadcast values stay as they are).
- The FIXME on Activate (correct as it is) is dropped.

The todo_wine for IKsPropertySet in the audio path test is removed.
